          "type": "turn_end",
          "turn": {
            "text": "Alberto's Fraud Detection Agent is built for an online event ticketing platform. It reviews newly published events and organizers, then gives a human admin an approve, reject, or request-info recommendation along with the reasons.\n\nIt uses graded autonomy: it auto-approves only when the evidence is verified in code, and web sources can hold a decision back but can never approve one.\n\nThe project is at the offline-evals stage. In 31 test cases, the team tried a local 9B model and then chose Claude Haiku 5.5 for deployment. Haiku reached 86% accuracy (vs. 71% for the local model), approved 1% of fraud cases (vs. 8%), and costs about $0.002 per review. The stack is TypeScript, PostgreSQL and GCP.",
